          %h1#section_table_of_contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#explicit_definition"} Explicit definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_pages"} Related pages
              %li
                %a{:href => "#reference"} Reference
          %p
            An
            %strong anabicategory
            is a particular notion of
            %em
              weak
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            appropriate in the absence of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            (including in many
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal
            contexts). It is derived from the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            by replacing the composition functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \circ: B(y,z) \times B(x,y) \to B(x,z)
            with
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor"} anafunctor
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associator"} associator
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitor"} unitor
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ananatural+transformation"} ananatural transformations
          %p
            If
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            is defined as consisting of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"}> small
            )
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ananatural+transformation"} ananatural transformations
            (as is most appropriate in the absence of choice), then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            is more naturally an anabicategory rather than any stricter notion.
          %p
            Under the equivalence between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctors"} anafunctors
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+profunctors"} representable profunctors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+multicategory"} representable
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probicategories"} probicategories
          %h2#explicit_definition Explicit definition
          %p
            An anabicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            consists of a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_0
            of objects, a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_1
            of 1-cells, which are relations
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_0 \times \mathcal{C}_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_2
            of 2-cells, which are relations
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_1 \times \mathcal{C}_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_2
            needs a defined equality relation, so the other two sets only need to be
            = succeed "s.)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preset"} preset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            if we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x, y)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            is said to be a
            %em value
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x, y)
            are also said to be
            = succeed ";" do
              %em specified values
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            has some value at
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
          %ol
            %li
              There are
              %em source
              and
              %em target
              relations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_1 \times \mathcal{C}_0
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_2 \times \mathcal{C}_1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              has some specified value for its source and target.
            %li
              There are
              %em 2-source
